{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order","id":1027553,"title":"[2E] Multinational Status in Order","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T05:30:31-08:00","id":1027553,"title":"[2E] Multinational Status in Order","content":"To my London/globetrotting game about Earth's Chakras join player with Moros Libertine character of Treasure Hunter that sell his found Artifacts and Grimoires from Temples of Time Before to highest bidder, often to Free Council Lorehouses. As he jumps around the world and sell items to members of many Consilia - it would be good if his <i>Status ( Free Council ) 3</i> work in any of that locations. And I have many other characters that could benefit from shared Status, beside their home Consilium.<br /> <br /> I know that Mysterium has <i>Egregore</i> 2 Merit that let members to use full Status in<b> any</b> Order Caucus in the world. <b>But what about rest of Orders? Maybe some special Merit that let you use one dot lower Status than your home Consilium?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:56:12-08:00","id":1027569,"title":"","content":"What Egregore does is not actually expanding your Status. It allows other Mysterium members to recognize you. It's the reconition that allows you to use your full Status. If you manage to convince the new area that you are who you claim you are you would already gain the full Status without the need for an extra Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:09:10-08:00","id":1027575,"title":"","content":"If you do that you're removing one of the more valuable pieces of Egregore from the merit. The Mysterium are explicitly the ambassadors between the Orders internationally because of the Egregore. That said, inter-Order actions between Caucuses can probably be handled by using your Status in your home Caucus to requisition some sort of symbol of status that can be presented to another Caucus to vouch for your character and if they practice the Rite of Emeritus they'll respect you for your Status in your home town.<br /> <br /> If you're from a SL Caucus and you want to get in good with an Arrow Caucus in another country then you'd go to your Mysterium buddy for a voucher and in the other country your first stop would be the Mysterium Caucus so they could verify you via the Egregore and they would introduce you to the Arrow Caucus since the Arrows know their local Mysterium better than they know you. Then you might be able to use some of your AA Status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-06-2017, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:24:14-08:00","id":1027587,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a rule that specified that you act at - 2 Status when outside of your local community or something? I'm AFK, so I can't check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:48:32-08:00","id":1027605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027587#post1027587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a rule that specified that you act at - 2 Status when outside of your local community or something? I'm AFK, so I can't check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I readed in detail in Consilium/Order Status in 2E corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p. 100</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Orders are both global organizations and locally compartmentalized. If a character uses Order Status in a Caucus other than her home one, reduce her effective rating in this Merit by \u20131 if the Caucus is a member of the same Consilium or Assembly, \u20132 if it is a member of the same Convocation, and \u20133 if it is unrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, by RAW, it's okay to just go to your neighbors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But as my PCs generally do not have more than Status 3 in any Order and Consilium, this rule making it totally usefulness to have higher Status in global games.<br /> <br /> I understand from where it's coming ( used something like this for 1E games ), but that way it's not just work in gloe hoping in 2E. Some custom made Merit is in order ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027575#post1027575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do that you're removing one of the more valuable pieces of Egregore from the merit. The Mysterium are explicitly the ambassadors between the Orders internationally because of the Egregore. That said, inter-Order actions between Caucuses can probably be handled by using your Status in your home Caucus to requisition some sort of symbol of status that can be presented to another Caucus to vouch for your character and if they practice the Rite of Emeritus they'll respect you for your Status in your home town.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No, making custom Merit is not making 'Mysterium bad' - <i>Egregore</i> global advantage is only one part of 5 point Style-like chain, there is also 4 other advantages from this Merit. Also, every Mysterygouge can have it just by going deep in to Order. Rest of mages would be restricted by custom Merit requirements.<br /> <br /> 2. 'Mysterium as being only ambassadors of Diamon' could work to maybe 1800, but in era of fast travel and instant communication, it's very thick thread sewn. Cellphone call / Telepatic connection between your home Caucus leader and you guesting Caucus should solve 'viability' the same way as Mystygouges word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027575#post1027575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're from a SL Caucus and you want to get in good with an Arrow Caucus in another country then you'd go to your Mysterium buddy for a voucher and in the other country your first stop would be the Mysterium Caucus so they could verify you via the Egregore and they would introduce you to the Arrow Caucus since the Arrows know their local Mysterium better than they know you. Then you might be able to use some of your AA Status.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Libertine at heart&gt; Or you could simply call. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-06-2017, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:55:51-08:00","id":1027614,"title":"","content":"Instead of doing a Merit, how about a Condition that allows you to apply more of your Status towards target community? One of reasons why I'm wary about creating Merits for everything is that having too many Merits available &quot;at once&quot; isn't actually healthy for a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:57:46-08:00","id":1027617,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm sure that a Mage from another Caucus would be totally open to spells cast on him by strangers. /Sarcasm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:02:18-08:00","id":1027620,"title":"","content":"First draft of custom Merit for topic problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Well Travelled (</b>\u2022 to \u2022\u2022<b>) </b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Awakened, Status ( Order ) 2<br /> <b>Effect: </b> Your character has traveled to many Caucuses of his Order and recognized in all of them. Or she made very important actions for it, that her inter-Order fame is proceeding her. One way or another, she is known in locations outside her home Consilium. Her effective rating is one level higher than normally would be for each dot of this Merit. So on <i>Well Travelled (\u2022)</i> she can used her Status in Order as in Caucus of her home Consilium as normal, will have -1 effective level if it is a member of the same Convocation, and -2 if it is unrelated. <i>Well Travelled (\u2022\u2022) </i>gives normal usage of Status everywhere in your home Convocation and only -1 if Caucus is unrelated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:07:04-08:00","id":1027624,"title":"","content":"Like...all of them? There are people who don't recognize famous celebrities, scientists and politicans. I don't think Mages would be any better in this regard (why a Russian Mage would care about some dude in USA?). I could see this as a modifier to on a roll to be recognized, though (which would in turn give you modified Connected Condition). Otherwise I'm hard pressed to see this in merit form without actually buying it for specific locations. Which is like...buying Status anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:07:17-08:00","id":1027625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027614#post1027614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of doing a Merit, how about a Condition that allows you to apply more of your Status towards target community? One of reasons why I'm wary about creating Merits for everything is that having too many Merits available &quot;at once&quot; isn't actually healthy for a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can work if you want just to check every place characters are, and make all the stalking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> wants, in game. But if you run totally global game ( like chronicle I have in mind ), it will be unnecessary cluttering of Conditions on char sheet.<br /> <br /> Also, for <i>Well Traveled</i> to be usable in the first place, you still need high Order rating in your home Caucus - so you need to be 'star of your Order' in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:19:34-08:00","id":1027629,"title":"","content":"I'd give them the Fame merit from the CoD core. The character is just well known outside their assembly, that doesn't mean they have real status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:23:52-08:00","id":1027632,"title":"","content":"Stalking doesn't mean what you think it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:57:09-08:00","id":1027656,"title":"","content":"Mechanically speaking, ALL characters can get benefits as like from Well Traveled just by investing in Status of their home Caucus. For example, Status 3 character wants to have impact on other Caucuses of his Order ( or just lend stuff from there ). She can get to Status 5 to have effective Status 2 on the rest of world. Or our Status 3 character can take Well Traveled 2 and have the same Status 2 on the rest of world - without being de facto head of her Order. I think that using just special Merit without needing to make players to run local Caucus is better way for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027629#post1027629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd give them the Fame merit from the CoD core. The character is just well known outside their assembly, that doesn't mean they have real status.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fame Merit is really Sleepers thing in <b>Mage</b>. It highers your Sympathy connections from all the the people thinking about it. It has nothing to recognition in your Order. Mage/Celebrity can have Fame 3 because he plays in Hollywood, but still be just Status 1 in Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-06-2017, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:12:24-08:00","id":1027672,"title":"","content":"Wrong, Fame applies to a subset of society, Fame 3 could easily be characterized as world-wide fame with Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:27:46-08:00","id":1027822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027656#post1027656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that using just special Merit without needing to make players to run local Caucus is better way for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 5-dot magisters generally don't run caucuses. That's more for the 3-4 dot people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fame Merit is really Sleepers thing in <b>Mage</b>. It lowers your Sympathy connections from all the the people thinking about it. It has nothing to recognition in your Order. Mage/Celebrity can have Fame 3 because he plays in Hollywood, but still be just Status 1 in Order. </div> </div> </div>I actually said the one in the CoD core which doesn't have that stuff, but thinking on it, I'd actually have them use the Mage version. If you're that well known to the magi of the world, then yeah it makes perfect sense that it'd mess with your sympathies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T14:44:38-08:00","id":1027855,"title":"","content":"Still, Fame 3, even in Order circles, will not provide you in guesting Caucus like in home Caucus based on you Status. I mean things mention by Order Status Merit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p. 100</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character\u2019s position affords her certain access to her Caucus or Consilium\u2019s stores. She can access Artifacts, Imbued Items, mentors, libraries, Grimoires, and other magical resources. The Storyteller should assign an Availability rating to the item your character seeks, related to the power level or regular Merit rating. Consider your character\u2019s Status dots as Resources for the purpose of procuring these magical resources (see Acquiring Services, p. 228). Availability ratings assume the service or Merit will be assigned on a temporary basis (for a single story); add \u2022\u2022 for permanent requisitions. The group assumes she\u2019ll return it when done with it, or make amends if it\u2019s destroyed or lost. Merits suitable for requisition include Alternate Identity, Retainer, Imbued Item, Artifact, Grimoire, Mentor, Hallow, Sanctum, Library, Advanced Library, Safe Place, Familiar, and Resources, all with Availability equal to their dot rating. The Storyteller decides if your character\u2019s group has access to a particular magical resource; rank doesn\u2019t summon magical storehouses into being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another problem with Fame Merit is with implication to Occultation Merit - in setting, you <i>could </i>possibly run Guardian that has high Status ( or have Well Traveled ) with high Occulation. Character will be not known en masse in the Order itself, but Epopts alone around Convocations will knew about his standing and mission as they will exchange info about him. And having Occulation, he cannot have Fame then. Or vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-06-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:34:08-08:00","id":1027874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027855#post1027855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, Fame 3, even in Order circles, will not provide you in guesting Caucus like in home Caucus based on you Status. I mean things mention by Order Status</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're a guest. You can't requisition stuff. You can ask and use your +3 fame bonus. To go back to your example, your Free Council guy is basically just known to a lot of people. They might like him, or think he's really great but he's still just a guest, not a member of the caucus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another problem with Fame Merit is with implication to Occultation Merit - in setting, you <i>could </i>possibly run Guardian that has high Status ( or have Well Traveled ) with high Occulation. Character will be not known en masse in the Order itself, but Epopts alone around Convocations will knew about his standing and mission as they will exchange info about him. And having Occulation, he cannot have Fame then. Or vice versa. </div> </div> </div>Then use the original version. Just narrow the group to Epopts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T22:57:41-08:00","id":1028048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027874#post1027874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you're a guest. You can't requisition stuff. You can ask and use your +3 fame bonus. To go back to your example, your Free Council guy is basically just known to a lot of people. They might like him, or think he's really great but he's still just a guest, not a member of the caucus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is problem with RAW - <b>WHY I cannot requisite stuff on Order's goals when i'm guest?</b> I'm memeber of FC, don't I? Beside 'every Caucus is his own little domain', idea seems... well, not silly, but not mashing with global take on Orders. All Free Council Caucuses works for common good, for the same tenets and generally, each one of them is having objectives tied to fight Hierarchy ( for example ). They <i>should</i> help one another, don't they?<br /> <br /> And, what's even more silly is that if you ARE super in local Status you <b>can</b> get things in other place, just like low ranking member. It's not like game says 'every Caucus is totally different and they do not cooperate' - no, Order Status let you work with every Caucus on Earth if you are high enough. So I just make <i>Well Traveled </i>Merit for those ensuring cooperation between Caucuses, as some are clearly doing it in setting, at least from time to time. If boss (Status 5 ) from NYC can go to London and be treated as respected member simply on his inter-Order 'fame' ( Status 2 ), there <i>should </i>be people in Orders that exchange those news and 'Status lists' between Caucuses. It's not very much stretch to assume those that exchange are less 'strangers' than rest of members to the Caucuses they visit. Think here more on traveling merchants between villages - they are still 'guests', but 'regular ones', working on much better standing than total foreigners in eyes of community.<br /> <br /> Saying 'use the Fame' is silly, as it is 'use other Merit that has some magical implications ( Sympathy rules ) that is not made strictly for things like Status, but do not go after house Merit that is doing almost the same on mechanics you look for without mixing original Merits goals'.<br /> <br /> So I have proposition - Maybe we stick to my <i>Well Traveled</i> Merit idea? Discussion do not seems to lead anywhere new and I still need to make sure on him is it balanced enough. Let's just assume I can do this things in my games and would most work with Merit, so I need help on balancing it, okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-07-2017, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T23:18:38-08:00","id":1028053,"title":"","content":"Why don't you just have a super-special Merit called &quot;Global Order Status&quot; and just use that instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T00:38:11-08:00","id":1028059,"title":"","content":"They should, but they don't. It's a world of chronicles of darkness. They will instead probably look at you suspiciously and hiss at you because your idea of revolution is different than theirs. Look at the Catholic Church and it's priests - theoretically, they are all members of one organization...and yet, individual priests are often extremely territorial and will look at new people in their area as competition, not as help.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you are the GM. You can just make a homerule that states &quot;for purposes of this Chronicle, Status is fully and well global&quot;. No need to justify yourself by having community-approved merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T02:19:50-08:00","id":1028075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1028053#post1028053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't you just have a super-special Merit called &quot;Global Order Status&quot; and just use that instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm basically doing that. My <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027620#post1027620\"><i>Well Traveled</i> Merit idea</a> is it's just rise <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1027605#post1027605\">natural possible of usage of Order Status that is in the corebook</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1028059#post1028059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should, but they don't. It's a world of chronicles of darkness. They will instead probably look at you suspiciously and hiss at you because your idea of revolution is different than theirs. Look at the Catholic Church and it's priests - theoretically, they are all members of one organization...and yet, individual priests are often extremely territorial and will look at new people in their area as competition, not as help.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you are the GM. You can just make a homerule that states &quot;for purposes of this Chronicle, Status is fully and well global&quot;. No need to justify yourself by having community-approved merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm here torn on this, really. I think that idea for characters with truly global Status should be, but also I think the normal 'day to day' Caucus members will stick only to their home Caucus. Like I mentioned above - those 'multi-Caucus' members would be like traveling merchants of Orders - they are sorta special role in the society, most people just stay in their own village. As those 'one or two in community that truly travel', it sounds to me as Merit for characters.<br /> <br /> Also, making Mysterium members having this kind connections inside their Egregore, sounds they are more cool this way, so I do not want to over shine totally viability of Egregore 2 advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-07-2017, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:49:56-08:00","id":1028192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027553-2e-multinational-status-in-order?p=1028048#post1028048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is problem with RAW - <b>WHY I cannot requisite stuff on Order's goals when i'm guest?</b> I'm memeber of FC, don't I? Beside 'every Caucus is his own little domain', idea seems... well, not silly, but not mashing with global take on Orders. All Free Council Caucuses works for common good, for the same tenets and generally, each one of them is having objectives tied to fight Hierarchy ( for example ). They <i>should</i> help one another, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>For someone who has argued so hard for the continued existence of Nameless Orders I find it ironic that you're annoyed when the game is set up to encourage some level of residual independence in those organizations of Mages that finally bought a franchise. The Orders can't help it that they don't work together as well as they could, they have no centralized form of government so although their memetic makeup is easily transferable authority outside of their individual cells isn't.<br /> <br /> Another reason you can't requisition stuff if you're an outsider? They're using that stuff for -their- people and -their- problems, unless they're very lucky they don't have the manpower or means to cater to your every whim too when they have to be taking care of themselves. Besides, what have you ever done for them? You may have served the Order's overall mission, but that's not exactly contributing on a meaningful, personal level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}